# ~/.claude/repo-allowlist
#
# The answers you have given, one line per repo. Install this file EMPTY — comments
# only — and add a line the first time a repo asks you for one.
#
# It lives in ~/.claude/ and NOT in any repo, on purpose: a file inside the project is
# one the agent can write, and a guardrail the model can switch off is a suggestion with
# extra steps. PHILOSOPHY.md §5 is "enforced by the harness, not by trust".
#
# NOT LISTED MEANS NO TO BOTH. That is the whole design — a new repo is safe with no
# action from you, and a live project stays safe by omission rather than by being
# remembered.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT: three whitespace-separated fields.
#
#   <remote-fragment>            <push>   <own-claude-md>
#
#   remote-fragment   matched as a SUBSTRING of `git config --get remote.origin.url`,
#                     so one line covers the SSH and HTTPS forms of the same repo.
#                     Keyed by REMOTE, never by folder path — what push risks is where
#                     the content goes, and a path is the rule-about-paths mistake this
#                     whole design exists to retire. Make it specific enough not to
#                     match a repo you did not mean: "github.com/you/thing", not "you".
#   push              may the agent run `git push` here?          yes | no
#   own-claude-md     is this repo's CLAUDE.md its own — that is, would a fresh clone
#                     on a new laptop need it?                    yes | no
#
# Anything that is not exactly `yes` is no.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two things this file cannot switch off, whatever it says:
#
#   * `git add -A` / `git add .` stays blocked everywhere. The accidental sweep is the
#     case the guardrail was really written for.
#   * `.claude/` (except `agents/` and `skills/`), `.serena`, `.forgetful` and MEMORY.md
#     stay blocked everywhere. Those are your machine, not the project.
#
# See docs/solo/07-guardrails-when-solo.md for why each answer is the shape it is.
#
# Example — delete or keep commented; an empty file is the correct starting state:
#
# github.com/you/weekend-project    yes    yes
# github.com/you/photo-organiser    yes    yes
